            <div xml:id="d616">

                <pb facs="0872" n="758" xml:id="pg758"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1416: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morgan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-10-09T12:00:00-02:00">October 9,
                        1931—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received October 9—11:20 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>70. Brazilian Minister for Foreign Affairs showed me an hour ago the text of a
                    telegram received yesterday from Gracie, Brazilian Minister in La Paz, reporting
                    that the Chief of Staff of the Bolivian Army had stated to him that the said
                    army proposes aggressive action against Paraguay, occupation of Chaco forts on
                    Paraguayan frontier, and bombardment by airplanes of Asunción.</p>
                <p>Although selected, the names of the two Bolivian delegates to the November
                    conference in Washington have not yet been published.</p>
                <p>It would appear that the military party by aggressive action intends to prevent
                    the meeting of the conference or at least to obstruct its work.</p>
                <p>Brazilian Minister for Foreign Affairs considers the situation critical and that
                    only strong action by the powers which can influence Bolivian opinion must be
                    taken to prevent an open rupture and a state of war. He would like to know the
                    character of your advices and what cooperative action he may take with the
                    Five-Power Commission.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
